# The 500: Russian novels, stories, plays-in-verse and poems a Russian reader
# would name — the school programme (школьная программа) first, then the
# wider canon of the Golden and Silver Ages. Built Oct 2026.
#
# ONLY works that can be public domain on both sites are listed:
#   * Russia: the author died long enough ago (life + 70, +4 for the war years)
#     and was not posthumously rehabilitated late — Gumilyov, Mandelstam,
#     Kharms, Pilnyak are left out for that reason. Wikisource settles it in
#     the end: it hosts only what is public domain in Russia, so a work the
#     resolver cannot find there is simply not imported.
#   * USA (Samovar): published in 1930 or earlier, or by an author who died
#     by 1945 (out of copyright in Russia on the URAA date, so never restored).
#
# (author as the catalogue writes it, Wikisource surname marker, title, kind)
# kind: novel | novella | story | play | poem | fable | tale (verse fairy tale)
W = []
def add(author, marker, kind, *titles):
    for t in titles:
        W.append((author, marker, t, kind))

